---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import workshop from "../assets/screenshots/setlists.png";
const columns = [
  ["My setlists", "Every set kept in Music ▸ DubStemMix ▸ Setlists. New, rename, duplicate, delete. A setlist kept elsewhere can be moved in."],
  ["Library", "Every project in your DubStemMix and stems folders, with tempo and length, and a search. Drop a .dubstem to add one from elsewhere."],
  ["The set", "Drag songs in where you want them, drag lines to reorder. Never the same song twice. A colour and a tag per line, for this set only."],
];
---
<Section id="setlists" index="07" title="Build a set" kicker="the setlist workshop: plan at home, play at the dance">
  <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-cream/90">
    <strong>EDIT</strong> on the sidebar's setlist (or File ▸ Setlists…) opens the workshop in place of the console. Listen to any
    song with ▶, raw and without effects, and click in its waveform to jump anywhere. Every change is saved; <strong>LOAD IN THE
    CONSOLE</strong> takes the set back to the board.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
    {columns.map(([title, text]) => (
      <li class="rounded border-[1.5px] border-border bg-surface p-4">
        <p class="label-wide text-sm">{title}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">{text}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <figure class="mt-10">
    <Image src={workshop} alt="DubStemMix setlist workshop: my setlists, the library, a set with colours and tags, one song being listened to" width={1440} format="webp" loading="lazy" class="w-full border border-border" />
    <figcaption class="mono mt-3 text-[11px] text-dim">The setlist workshop: a colour and a tag per line, ▶ to listen before you add.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-dim">
    During the set, the sidebar stays the setlist you play. A request? <span class="text-cream">+</span> slips any song in just after
    the one playing, without touching the music. Tunes played for 30 seconds are greyed with a ✓. A song whose project moved shows
    in red: right-click ▸ Locate….
  </p>
</Section>
